The decision SHALL take into account:

* the authenticated identity, the role, the organization and the purpose of use of the requester, as conveyed in the access token (see [Get Access Token [ITI-71]](iti-71.html));
* for health professionals and health institutions, their entry in the directory of health professionals and health institutions (see [Find Matching Care Services [ITI-90]](iti-90.html)) and the treatment context they assert;
* the rights by law and the consents in effect for the holder concerned, including those defined by a representative;
* the confidentiality level of the data concerned.

In addition, the Policy Repository SHALL verify that:

* the patient of the consent (`Consent.patient`) is the patient of the access token (`person_id`);
* for the role `ADM`, the community of the administration (`subject_organization_id`) manages the health dossier (`Consent.organization` of the [opening](ppqm-consent.html#consent-opening)), and, except for the [legal representative](ppqm-consent.html#consent-legal-representative) and for adding a [community mandate](ppqm-consent.html#consent-community-mandate), a community mandate of the holder for that community is in effect;
* for the role `REP`, the [representative](ppqm-consent.html#consent-representative) consent of the representative is in effect and grants the action required by the consent type (see the notes of Table 3 of [Who May Record and Retrieve Which Consent](ppqm-consent.html#who-may-record-and-retrieve-which-consent));
* for the roles `HCP` and `ASS`, the health professional the request is made for, or the group or health institution in `group_id`, is the grantee of an [indirect authorization](ppqm-consent.html#consent-indirect-authorization), and the grantee of the access right a [delegation](ppqm-consent.html#consent-delegation) is derived from;
* the `performer` of the consent corresponds to the requester:

| | |
| :--- | :--- |
| `PAT`, also a digital health application acting for the holder | The holder (EPR-SPID =`person_id`) |
| `REP`,`LEGREP` | The representative or legal representative (representative ID =`user_id`).[Community mandate](ppqm-consent.html#consent-community-mandate)added by the legal representative: the legal representative |
| `HCP`,`ASS` | [Indirect authorization](ppqm-consent.html#consent-indirect-authorization): the holder.[Delegation](ppqm-consent.html#consent-delegation): the health professional (GLN of the health professional the request is made for), or the group or health institution (`group_id`) |
| `ADM` | [Legal representative](ppqm-consent.html#consent-legal-representative): the community or authority.[Community mandate](ppqm-consent.html#consent-community-mandate): the holder or the legal representative who gave the mandate. Other consent types, on mandate: the holder |

Table 1: Performer of the consent by the role of the requester

The Policy Repository SHALL also record an audit event for every consent it adds, deletes or updates itself under the Policy Repository rules:

* where the rule is applied because of the request of a user, according to the Delete or Update profile above, with the user of that request as main user and the `traceparent` of that request: the delegations derived from a revoked access right, the indirect authorizations deleted when the indirect authorization is excluded, the consents of the holder deleted when a legal representative is set up, and the access rights updated when a document is purged;
* where no user is involved, with the Policy Repository as initiating agent: the consents added when the health dossier is opened according to [CH Audit Event for the addition of a consent by the Policy Repository](StructureDefinition-ChAuditEventPpq3RepositoryCreate.html) ([example for the emergency access setting](AuditEvent-ChAuditEventPpq3RepositoryCreateExample.html)), and the consents deleted according to [CH Audit Event for the deletion of a consent by the Policy Repository](StructureDefinition-ChAuditEventPpq3RepositoryDelete.html) with the reason of the deletion ([example for an access right deleted on the death of the holder](AuditEvent-ChAuditEventPpq3RepositoryDeleteExample.html)): `dissolution` and `death` for the consents deleted when the health dossier is dissolved.
